#front-door
(name *)        front door
(* is #in #west-of-house)
(prevent [enter *])
    (narrate door is locked)
(prevent [open *])
    The door cannot be opened.
(prevent [unlock *])
    It doesn't seem to work.
%% Check going east from West of House: say "The door is locked, and there is evidently no key." instead.

#white-house
(name *)        white house
(#west-of-house attracts *)
(#north-of-house attracts *)
(#south-of-house attracts *)
(#east-of-house attracts *)
(descr *)
    The house is a beautiful colonial house which is painted white.
    It is clear that the owners must have been extremely wealthy.

#north-of-house
(name *)        North of House
(room *)
(outdoors *)
(from * go #west to #west-of-house)
(from * go #east to #east-of-house)
(from * go #north to #forest3)
(narrate failing to leave * #south)
    (narrate windows are barred)
(look *)
    You are facing the north side of a white house.
    There is no door here, and all the windows are barred.

#south-of-house
(name *)        South of House
(room *)
(outdoors *)
(from * go #west to #west-of-house)
(from * go #east to #east-of-house)
(from * go #south to #forest2)
(narrate failing to leave * #north)
    (narrate windows are barred)
(look *)
    You are facing the south side of a white house.
    There is no door here, and all the windows are barred.

#east-of-house
(name *)        Behind House
(room *)
(outdoors *)
(from * go #north to #north-of-house)
(from * go #south to #south-of-house)
(from * go #east to #clearing)
(look *)
    You are behind the white house.
    In one corner of the house is a window that is
    (if)(#window is open)(then)
        slightly ajar.
    (else)
        open.
    (endif)

#window
(name *)        window
(door *)
(openable *)
(from #east-of-house go #west through #window to #kitchen)
(from #kitchen go #east through #window to #east-of-house)
(* blocks passage)
	(* is closed)
(perform [climb *])
    (try [enter *])
(narrate opening *)
    With great effort, you open the window far enough to allow entry.
(narrate closing *)
    The window closes \(more easily than it opened\).

#kitchen
(name *)        Kitchen
(room *)
(from * go #west to #living-room)
(from * go #up to #attic)
(look *)
    This is the kitchen of the white house.
    A table seems to have been used recently for the preparation of food.
    A passage leads to the west and a dark staircase can be seen leading upward.
    A dark chimney leads down and to the east is a small window which is
    (if)(#window is open)(then)
        open.
    (else)
        closed.
    (endif)
(prevent [go #down])
    (current room *)
    Only Santa Claus climbs down chimneys.
(move player to #in *)
    (* is unvisited)
    (increase score by 10)
    (fail)

#sack
