%% Readable objects print their description when you read them.
(perform [read $thing])
    (readable $thing)
    (try [take $thing])
    It reads:
    (par)
    (look $thing)

#newspaper
(* is #in #living-room)
(name *)        newspaper
(item *)
(size *)        2
(readable *)
(dict *)        news paper issue report magazine
(appearance *)
    There is an issue of US NEWS & DUNGEON REPORT dated 7/25/2026 here.
(descr *)
    (line)            US NEWS & DUNGEON REPORT
    (line)7/25/2026                                     Late Dungeon Edition
    (line)
    (line)FLASH!
    (line)    We'll let you know about bugs as they are discovered or squashed.

%%%

(forest name)   Forest
(forest look)
    You are in a forest, with trees in all directions around you.
(forest look east)
    You are in a dimly lit forest, with large trees all around.  To the
    east, there appears to be sunlight.

#forest1
(room *)
(outdoors *)
(name *)    (forest name)
(look *)   (forest look)
(from * go #north to #forest1)
(from * go #east to #forest3)
(from * go #south to #forest2)
(from * go #west to #forest1)

#forest2
(room *)
(outdoors *)
(name *)    (forest name)
(look *)   (forest look east)
(from * go #north to #south-of-house)
(from * go #east to #clearing)
(from * go #south to #forest4)
(from * go #west to #forest1)

#forest3
(room *)
(outdoors *)
(name *)    (forest name)
(look *)   (forest look east)
(from * go #north to #forest2)
(from * go #east to #clearing)
(from * go #south to #clearing)
(from * go #west to #north-of-house)

#forest4
(room *)
(outdoors *)
(name *)    (forest name)
(look *)
    You are in a large forest, with trees obstructing all views except
    to the east, where a small clearing may be seen through the trees.
(from * go #north to #forest5)
(from * go #east to #cliff-top)
(from * go #south to #forest4)
(from * go #west to #forest2)

#forest5
(room *)
(outdoors *)
(name *)    (forest name)
(look *)   (forest look)
(from * go #north to #forest5)
(from * go #southeast to #cliff-top)
(from * go #south to #forest4)
(from * go #west to #forest2)

#clearing
(room *)
(outdoors *)
(name *)    Clearing
(look *)
    You are in a clearing, with a forest surrounding you on the west
    and south.
(from * go #southwest to #east-of-house)
(from * go #southeast to #forest5)
(from * go #north to #clearing)
(from * go #east to #clearing)
(from * go #west to #forest3)
(from * go #south to #forest2)
(from * go #down through #grating to #grating-room)
    ~(#grating is #under #pile-of-leaves)
(narrate failing to leave * #down)
    The grating is locked.

#pile-of-leaves
(name *)    pile of leaves
(item *)
(appearance *)
    There is a pile of leaves on the ground.
(* is #in #clearing)
(after [take *])
    (#grating is #under #pile-of-leaves)
    A grating appears on the ground.
    (now)(#grating is #in #clearing)
    (notice #grating)
(after [look #under *])
    (#grating is #under #pile-of-leaves)
    (now)(#grating is #in #clearing)
    (notice #grating)

#grating
(name *)    grating
(openable *)
(lockable *)
(* is hidden)
(* is #under #pile-of-leaves)
(appearance *)
    (if)(* is open)(then)
        There is an open grating, descending into darkness.
    (else)
        There is a grating securely fastened into the ground.
    (endif)

#cliff-top
(room *)
(outdoors *)
(name *)        Canyon View
(look *)
    You are at the top of the Great Canyon on its south wall.  From here
    there is a marvelous view of the Canyon and parts of the Frigid River
    upstream.  Across the canyon, the walls of the White Cliffs still
    appear to loom far above.  Following the Canyon upstream \(north and
    northwest\), Aragain Falls may be seen, complete with rainbow. 
    Fortunately, my vision is better than average and I can discern the
    top of the Flood Control Dam \#3 far to the distant north.  To the
    west and south can be seen an immense forest, stretching for miles
    around.  It is possible to climb down into the canyon from here.
(from * go #down to #cliff-mid)
(from * go #south to #forest4)
(from * go #west to #forest5)

#cliff-mid
(room *)
(outdoors *)
(name *)        Rocky Ledge
(look *)
    You are on a ledge about halfway up the wall of the river canyon.
    You can see from here that the main flow from Aragain Falls twists
    along a passage which it is impossible to enter.  Below you is the
    canyon bottom.  Above you is more cliff, which still appears
    climbable.
(from * go #up to #cliff-top)
(from * go #down to #cliff-bottom)

#cliff-bottom
(room *)
(outdoors *)
(name *)        Canyon Bottom
(look *)
    You are beneath the walls of the river canyon which may be climbable
    here.  There is a small stream here, which is the lesser part of the
    runoff of Aragain Falls. To the north is a narrow path.
(from * go #up to #cliff-mid)
(from * go #north to #end-of-rainbow)

#end-of-rainbow
(room *)
(outdoors *)
(name *)        End of Rainbow
(look *)
    You are on a small beach on the continuation of the Frigid River
    past the Falls.  The beach is narrow due to the presence of the White
    Cliffs.  The river canyon opens here and sunlight shines in from
    above. A rainbow crosses over the falls to the west and a narrow path
    continues to the southeast.
(from * go #southeast to #cliff-bottom)

#rainbow
(room *)
(outdoors *)
(name *)        Rainbow Room
(look *)
    You are on top of a rainbow \(I bet you never thought you would walk
    on a rainbow\), with a magnificent view of the Falls.  The rainbow
    travels east-west here.  There is an NBC Commissary here.
(from * go #east to #end-of-rainbow)
(from * go #west to #falls)

%%%

#cellar
(name *)        Cellar
(room *)
(inherently dark *)
(look *)
    You are in a dark and damp cellar with a narrow passageway leading
    east, and a crawlway to the south.  On the west is the bottom of a
    steep metal ramp which is unclimbable.
(narrate failing to leave * #up)
    The trap door has been barred from the other side.
(narrate failing to leave * #west)
    You try to ascend the ramp, but it is impossible, and you slide back down.

%%%

(narrate darkness)
    It is pitch black.  You are likely to be eaten by a grue.
    (notice #grue)

#grue
(name *)    lurking grue
%%TODO
(descr *)
    The grue is a sinister, lurking presence in the dark places of the
    earth.  Its favorite diet is adventurers, but its insatiable
    appetite is tempered by its fear of light.  No grue has ever been
    seen by the light of day, and few have survived its fearsome jaws
    to tell the tale.
(prevent [find *])
    There is no grue here, but I'm sure there is at least one lurking
    in the darkness nearby.  I wouldn't let my light go out if I were
    you!

%%%

(understand [repent] as [repent])
(refuse [repent])
    It could very well be too late!

%% Not exactly like Zork
(list contents of $thing)
    (if){ ($thing is open) (or) ~(opaque $thing) }(then)
        (line)
        (list objects #in $thing)
        (list objects #on $thing)
        (list objects #under $thing)
    (endif)

%% Default rule - Look at a thing that is an openable container
(descr $thing)
    (container $thing)
    (openable $thing)
    (The $thing) is (if)($thing is open)(then)open(else)closed(endif).
    (list contents of $thing)
